<title>UK: Bank of New York wins May Reuter Forex poll.</title>
<headline>Bank of New York wins May Reuter Forex poll.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of New York in London won the Reuter foreign exchange poll for May, beating 35 other contenders from across the globe in the monthly contest.</p>
<p>The average divergence of Bank of New York's exchange rate predictions from the actual rates at the end of the month was 1.27 percent.</p>
<p>Paine Webber International in London came second with a divergence of 1.94 percent followed, closely, in third place by BG Bank in Copenhagen with an average divergence of 1.96 percent.</p>
<p>Overall, the percentage difference between the actual and forecast rates varied between 1.27 and 4.79 percent.</p>
<p>The rankings were based on the accuracy of the forecasts against the European closing rates on May 30 of Dollar/mark at 1.7087, dollar/yen at 116.42 and sterling/dollar at 1.6365.</p>
